`SensorArchive` must snapshot the constructor array and every reading object. `byZone` compares the trimmed query to stored trimmed zone names case-sensitively and preserves constructor order. An empty query throws `Error`; no matches returns `[]`. `newest` throws `Error` for an empty query or no matching reading. It returns the matching reading with the greatest sequence number; ties are resolved in favor of the earlier constructor entry. Sequence numbers must be non-negative safe integers, and zones must be non-empty after trimming. Invalid constructor input throws without retaining caller-owned state. Every returned reading must be a fresh object, so caller mutation cannot alter the archive.

